WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.400
I had to transition

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:06.375
The company was just sold

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.184
So we had to move out of
Symantec into our own space

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.010
And went through a full RFB with different

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.030
Cloud providers as well
as data center providers

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:25.200
And came to a realization IBM Cloud and VMware
was the right solution for Veritas

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.780
IBM was the first one that
actually had the offering

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:35.080
Both on bare metal as well
as the VM stack and VM cloud

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.820
It was the only solution
that made sense

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.020
Nobody else offered the
spectrum of the options

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:46.480
I'm hybrid

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.940
But 95% in the cloud

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.580
I really wanted to
have a very seamless migration

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.380
To anywhere, because the
company was already live

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.980
The open architecture
that IBM Cloud provided

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:03.120
The bare metal that IBM Cloud
provided, it allowed me to

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.840
Both use our own product, Veritas product

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:11.040
and VMware tools to be
able to move live work load

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.900
With minimal to no impact to our business

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.460
On a Friday night go home

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:19.600
And by Monday morning they
come in and everything is working

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.920
They don't even know that I moved them

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.240
That was important

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.480
The big win for IT is

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:29.480
Not to interrupt the business

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:38.580
We moved 95% of our enterprise
applications into IBM Cloud

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:42.000
Both on the bare metal and VMware

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.360
and out of the thousand workloads running on IBM Cloud

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:52.340
Out of those, 80%, 90% of it is running on VMware

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:58.720
and the other 10% to 20% is running on bare metal servers

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:04.000
Even though I'm on the public cloudI have the security of a virtual private cloud

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.080
Being the Chief Security Officer

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.040
It enables me to have
a little bit more sleep

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.160
The bare metal is
being the key for me

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.920
But we have lots of applications
that have been there forever

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.200
Now the next journey is the
application modernization

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.600
To truly make them
cloud-aware and utilize

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.080
The services that is available to us

